// BUG REPRO (Timepoint summand): the aggregation summand — the variable whose
// values are added together — must be a `Long`. Here `sum t` adds together
// `t`, which is declared `Timepoint`. Timepoints are ordinal positions, not
// quantities, so summing them is meaningless (and the two backends disagree on
// it). A `Timepoint` is legitimate in the `for (…)` binders — it controls
// per-timepoint row distinctness — but not as the value being summed.
//
// The summand's type was never checked: `collect_declared_binders` records only
// the `for_vars` into the type env, and `term_type(Agg)` hard-codes the whole
// aggregate to `int`, so a non-Long summand validated cleanly. This should be
// rejected by the temporal type-checker.
//
// Expected: rejected at `validate`.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when temporal {
    exists (n: Long). (
        (sum t for (t: Timepoint). where (Drupe::Action::"Charge"::request{} && tp(t))) == n
        && n > 0
    )
};
